{
  "id": "greybox-01",
  "format": 1,
  "$comment": "T-4.09: greybox-01 as a level of free boxes (level format v1, `sim/level.ts`), moved from data/worlds/ unchanged in every box and number: it expands to the same World, so its committed navmesh and cover bake still match. `pieces` places kit pieces from the asset manifest at a quarter turn; `encounter` names its encounter file. From T-3.31: T-3.31. The grey-box mission map: a fixture for M3's exit gate, not E-4.3's level format. Boxes as in range.json (x/z the centre, y the BOTTOM, w/h/d full sizes, metres). +z is up-range, as on the range, and the squad starts on the same spawn line (z = -6, x -3.75..3.75, `SPAWN_POINTS`), so `mission.start` is drawn round it. A 4 m spine (x -3..3, z 8..58) splits the ground into two lanes, walled on the outside at x = ±32: the WEST lane is the overwatch route — open, long sight lines up its length, a few low walls to go prone or crouch behind; the EAST lane is the assault route — four 17 m high walls from alternate sides (z 13, 25, 38, 50) that zigzag it, so no line runs far up it, with crates and low walls between: close cover all the way. Two low walls by the start cover both routes' first legs. Both come out behind the spine at z 58 and go round the objective compound (x -8..8, z 64..76, 2.4 m walls) to its two side doors (x = ±8, z 69..71.5): west door for overwatch, east for assault. `mission.routes[].via` are the points a route is walked through, in order, from the start's centre to the objective's; `minDistinctShare` is how much of each route's length (sampled every `sampleM` along its navmesh path) must lie on polygons the other route never touches; `coverWithinM` is how near a baked cover point counts as cover at a sample, and `maxUncoveredM` the longest stretch of a route with none; `sightM` is a clear eye-height sight line the overwatch route must have along itself, which the assault route must not. `spawnZones` are where enemies may appear (T-3.32): behind the objective and on each route, `on` naming which.",
